We are looking for an experienced Data Scientist to engage with Flix on a freelance/service agreement basis (B2B contract). This is a contractor engagement for a professional who wants to work on impactful, hands-on data science challenges like estimating price elasticity from noisy booking data, testing new demand signals, and turning a sound method into a model that runs in production. &nbsp;

Scope of Services

Bring expertise in&nbsp; data science and quantitative analysis &nbsp; to w ork within Flix's Revenue Management System and build demand forecasting and price elasticity models. &nbsp;

About the Engagement

• Further develop demand forecast and price elasticity models that drive automatic pricing across the Flix network &nbsp;

• Research and test improved approaches to modelling price elasticity -&nbsp;from first hypothesis to validated, production-ready model &nbsp;

• Act as a subject-matter expert partner&nbsp;for forecast and pricing models, advising product and business counterparts on problems, solution ideas, and feasibility &nbsp;

• Actively contribute your ideas to technical brainstorming and modelling discussions&nbsp;as advisor &nbsp;

• Effectively collaborate with others to implement solutions and ensure they are practical to operate reliably in production &nbsp;

• Monitor and analyse the behaviour of pricing products and respond to support cases &nbsp;

• Contribute to the technical health, reliability, and observability of the existing system &nbsp;

About You

• Strong academic background in mathematics, physics, statistics, operations research, quantitative economics, or a related field, with a solid grounding in statistics and data analysis &nbsp;

• Alternatively, proven hands-on expertise in price elasticity or demand modelling, for example from pricing or revenue management in transport, travel, hospitality or retail &nbsp;

• Critical thinking and attention to detail: You question assumptions, check your results and derive your own solutions in a complex environment. &nbsp;

• Programming experience - preferably Python; strong background in another language is acceptable &nbsp;

• Good SQL skills &nbsp;

• Basic knowledge of machine learning &nbsp;

• Strong communication skills to explain your approach and results clearly to technical and non-technical colleagues &nbsp;

• You implement your models yourself and care that they run reliably &nbsp;

• You enjoy working with others, and you can build resilient working relationships&nbsp;with your stakeholders, even in a remote setup

Cooperation model

• Cooperation based on a service agreement (B2B/freelance contract), not an employment contract.

• You will operate as an independent contractor, responsible for delivering agreed services and submitting invoices &nbsp;

• Location : open for contractors based in Poland

